{#- Atlas — one workstream (decisions 13, 14, 15, 21).

  The manifest is the authority for position, so everything on this page above the milestone table
  is read straight out of it. The milestone table is a table of contents for the plans, not a
  second copy of them: each row links to the milestone's own page.

  Decision 21: design entries are named, never linked and never rendered. CI cannot reach the
  design project, and anything only in the design project is by definition not approved — a link
  would imply otherwise.

  Data this layout expects:
    workstream — one { slug, dir, manifestPath, manifest } from resolveWorkstreams
    issues     — this workstream's open issues, i.e. fetchProjectIssues(...).byLabel for its label
                 (an empty list is fine, and is what a build with no GitHub reach produces)
    project, repo, title — see base.njk
-#}
{% extends "base.njk" %}
{% import "base.njk" as ui %}

{% block bodyClass %}page page-workstream{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Project depth</a></p>
<h1>{{ workstream.manifest.codename }} {{ ui.chip("stage", workstream.manifest.stage) }}</h1>
<p class="lede">{{ workstream.manifest.what }}</p>

<ul class="meta-list">
<li><span class="meta-label">Where it stands</span>{{ workstream.manifest.position }}</li>
<li><span class="meta-label">Label</span><code>{{ workstream.manifest.label }}</code></li>
</ul>

<p class="gate-callout"><span class="meta-label">Gate</span>{{ workstream.manifest.gate }}</p>

<h2>Milestones</h2>
{% if workstream.manifest.milestones | length %}
<div class="md-table-scroll">
<table class="records">
<thead>
<tr><th scope="col">Milestone</th><th scope="col">Title</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Issue</th><th scope="col">Pull request</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{% for entry in workstream.manifest.milestones %}
<tr>
<th scope="row" class="num"><a href="/workstream/{{ workstream.slug }}/{{ entry.id | lower }}/">{{ entry.label }}</a></th>
<td>{{ entry.title }}</td>
<td>{{ ui.chip("status", entry.status) }}</td>
<td class="num">{% if entry.issue %}<a href="https://github.com/{{ repo }}/issues/{{ entry.issue }}">#{{ entry.issue }}</a>{% else %}<span class="empty">None yet</span>{% endif %}</td>
<td class="num">{% if entry.pr %}<a href="https://github.com/{{ repo }}/pull/{{ entry.pr }}">#{{ entry.pr }}</a>{% else %}<span class="empty">None yet</span>{% endif %}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{% else %}
<p class="empty">No milestones on record yet.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Design</h2>
{% if workstream.manifest.design | length %}
<ul class="named-refs">
{% for reference in workstream.manifest.design %}
<li>{{ reference.name }} <span class="where">{{ reference.where }} — named, not rendered: CI cannot reach it, and nothing held only there is approved</span></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% else %}
<p class="empty">No design references on record.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Open issues</h2>
{% if issues | length %}
<ul class="issue-list">
{% for issue in issues %}
<li><a href="{{ issue.html_url }}"><span class="num">#{{ issue.number }}</span> {{ issue.title }}</a></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% else %}
<p class="empty">No open issues carry this workstream's label.</p>
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
